 "notes": "Generated-row sibling (#4507) of genapp-lgipdb01: CUSTOMER, POLICY and the ENDOWMENT / HOUSE / MOTOR / COMMERCIAL type tables are generated from base/cntl/db2cre.jcl (the same generate block as genapp-lgapdb01-generated: identity policy numbers 1000001..1000012, FKs POLICY->CUSTOMER and type->POLICY, NULLs and boundary values), not GenApp's INSERTs. The 32 generated requests are written against those rows (a request names a customer and a policy that the seed 4507 rows hold, or one they do not): 01IEND / 01IHOU / 01IMOT / 01ICOM found, wrong customer (+100 '01'), policy of another type (+100); 02ICOM by policy; 03ICOM Cust_Cursor (customer 1 holds two commercial policies, which the hand-seeded case never reached: the cursor loop runs twice), a customer with one and one with none; 05ICOM Zip_Cursor (a postcode held, one it does not, one in the wrong case); 04ICOM and 99XXXX are unknown request ids ('99'). A change to the generator's draw moves which policies exist: the E2E test in tests/cobol_mainframe/test_equivalence_db2_rows.py fails the case then (the SQLCODE mix and row counts it asserts move). Not generated: an endowment inquiry on policy 1000010, whose generated PADDINGDATA is empty (not NULL): CA-E-PADDING-DATA(1:0) is a zero-length reference modification (oracle_assumptions.md X8, libcob 'length out of bounds: 0'), the endowment path lgapdb01-generated leaves out too. The error paths (a negative SQLCODE on a SELECT, an OPEN or a CLOSE, the short COMMAREA '98') are genapp-lgipdb01's. Program, LINKed LGSTSQ and the LGCMAREA COMMAREA as in genapp-lgipdb01.",
